= Research and Projects

== CPU Performance and Bottleneck Analysis
My master's technical report, /Utilizing CPI Breakdown for Bottleneck Analysis of Power9 Processor Performance/, introduces an LDMS-Sampler framework for cycles-per-instruction (CPI) breakdown analysis and identifying performance bottlenecks in IBM Power9 processors. My work with Sandia National Laboratories included LDMS sampling toolkits for HPC data collection.

\[[https://tinyurl.com/cpibreakdown Technical report]] \[[https://github.com/ovis-hpc/ovis LDMS repository]]

== GPU Performance Prediction with Machine Learning
At New Mexico State University, I used NVBit-supported PPT-GPU to predict basic block counts for PolyBench, Rodinia, Pannotia, and LULESH workloads using machine learning. I also collaborated with Los Alamos National Laboratory on reuse distance and memory tracing toolkits for PPT-GPU.

Related publication: /BB-ML: Basic Block Performance Prediction using Machine Learning Techniques/ (2023). \[[publications.html Publications]] \[[https://github.com/lanl/PPT PPT repository]]

== GPU Design Verification
At Intel (July 2023 – September 2026), I worked on pre-silicon verification for discrete, integrated, and HPC GPUs. My work covered Intel Xe-Core ray tracing and texture sampling features, UVM-based validation, coverage closure, and functional debugging in simulation and emulation. During my graduate internship (May – December 2022), I worked on Xe-Core Sampler power analysis, Meteor Lake regressions, and UVM testbenches.

== Bachelor's Thesis: Secure IoT Automation
/A Secured Offline Online Approach for Internet of Things (IoT) Using Real-time Database/ presents IoT applications and a cyber-secured MQTT-based offline system with a shared dashboard for monitoring and control.

The related project with BUET and ACI Logistics Limited combined desktop software and a sensor network to monitor and control electrical appliances in a supershop. Our team developed and demonstrated the system, and I presented the resulting paper at WiSPNET in March 2019.

\[[https://tinyurl.com/y2n2qenu Thesis]] \[[pdf/hasan2019.pdf Paper]] \[[https://github.com/nh-turja/internet-of-things GitHub]]

~~~
