== Selected Engineering Projects
- *Design Validation using ASMD Diagram:* Debugged and verified hardware using an Algorithmic State Machine with Data Path diagram. \[[https://github.com/nh-turja/asmd_diagram_hw_sw_co_design_project GitHub]]
- *Cache Memory Simulator:* Developed C\+\+ programs to simulate direct-mapped and set-associative caches. \[[https://github.com/nh-turja/cache-simulator GitHub]]
- *MIPS:* Created a MIPS implementation using an Abstract Syntax Tree for the Compiler Transition course. \[[https://tinyurl.com/39dyv6zv GitHub]]
- *8-bit Simple As Possible (SAP) Computer:* Designed an 8-bit microcomputer with 64 KB of RAM and simulated it in Proteus. \[[https://github.com/nh-turja/simple-as-possible-computer GitHub]]
- *4-bit Shift Register:* Designed a general-purpose register supporting left shift, right shift, and parallel loading.
- *Wearable Device for Alzheimer's Patients:* Built a wearable device to help patients find their way inside a house. \[[https://tinyurl.com/y4mza8h9 GitHub]]

== Earlier Research and IoT Projects

=== Akita and Multi-GPU Simulation
My earlier work explored a multi-GPU simulation framework and benchmark development for evaluating next-generation multi-GPU system designs.

=== Railway Fishplate and Track Monitoring
In 2019, I worked with Professor Dr. Md Farhad Hossain at BUET on a proposal for an IoT railway monitoring system. The project received a 2020 grant from the University Grants Commission of Bangladesh. The proposed system aimed to detect and locate displaced fishplates and rail tracks, alert a central monitoring system, and display affected locations on a digital map.

=== Smart Waste Management
Our Team Hawkbit built an IoT waste management system for the 2018 CISCO Bangladesh hackathon, earning an honorable mention. The system sent bin status to a cloud server and used a SIM808 GSM module to send collection alerts.

~~~
{}{img_left}{photos/wastie/wastie.jpg}{Smart waste management project}{1000}{}
~~~

=== Smart Home Automation
Team Hawkbit won the Battle of Hardware (IoT) competition at BUET CSE Festival 2018. We built an Android app to monitor and control lights and fans, including brightness and fan speed, using MIT App Inventor and Google Firebase.

~~~
{}{img_left}{photos/boh/boh.jpg}{Battle of Hardware winning home automation project}{1000}{}
